From 0f94293aa68c17c57c074d9f3bcf4866fa7853d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:20:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Stub OpenAL: audio_core.cpp, openalsource.cpp/.h,
 openal.h

Real next-free slot for this content is 0023, not the "0024" PATCH-
SEQUENCE.md's table currently names it -- landed straight after 0022
(the SDL2_sound decoder stub) rather than after an intervening
ali3dsw.cpp window-surface patch, per this session's own explicit
option to go straight for the two audio stubs since they were the
confirmed next blockers. PLAN.md/PATCH-SEQUENCE.md get the
corresponding renumber in the same commit as the dosags-side patch
commit.

OpenAL/mojoAL is gated out of this port's link entirely by patch 0005
(FindLocalOpenAL.cmake's unconditional mojoAL fallback under a cross
compile); AL/al.h and AL/alc.h are never available to include. The
mojoAL-vs-custom-mixer decision for real audio is deferred to the
Sound milestone, same framing as patch 0022's SDL2_sound stub.

openal.h: gutted to an empty include-guarded header -- nothing in
openalsource.h/.cpp calls any al*/alc* function anymore, so there is
nothing left to declare (dump_al_errors() included; see below).

openalsource.h/.cpp: kept OpenAlSource's real public interface
(constructors, IsValid/GetPlayState/IsEmpty/GetPositionMs/PutData/Poll/
Play/Stop/Pause/Resume/SetPlaybackPosMs/SetPanning/SetSpeed/SetVolume)
so audio_core.cpp/audioplayer.cpp/.h -- none touched by this patch --
keep compiling against the same shape. PutData()/Poll() are now
unconditional no-ops (0/empty-queue) instead of touching a real device;
the PlayState state machine (Play/Stop/Pause/Resume) still transitions
the same way so GetPlayState() stays meaningful to any caller that
queries it, it just never has anything real to drive. Dropped every
member that only existed to talk to a real OpenAL source: _source
(ALuint), _alFormat (ALenum), _inputFmt/_recvFmt (Sound_AudioInfo --
see below), _resampler (SDLResampler), _bufferRecords/_queued and the
Unqueue() helper, plus the free-buffer pool (g_oalint) and the
OpenAlFormatFromSDLFormat()/GetBufferMs() helper functions -- all of
it existed purely to manage real OpenAL sources/buffers that no longer
exist here.

This also resolves the Sound_AudioInfo follow-on gap patch 0022's own
commit message flagged and deliberately left open for this patch:
openalsource.h no longer declares _inputFmt/_recvFmt at all, so
Sound_AudioInfo (an SDL2_sound type patch 0022 already removed the
only other source of) is no longer referenced anywhere in this file.

audio_core.cpp: audio_core_init()/audio_core_shutdown() no longer open/
close a real ALC device or context (alcOpenDevice/alcCreateContext/
alcMakeContextCurrent and their teardown counterparts all removed,
along with the three throw-on-failure checks that only made sense
against a real device). Also removed Sound_Init()/Sound_Quit()/
Sound_AvailableDecoders() decoder-enumeration calls -- direct SDL2_sound
API calls in this file, independent of SDLDecoder, not caught by patch
0022's own scope (which only touched sdldecoder.cpp/.h) and previously
masked by this same file's openal.h-triggered compile failure firing
first. dump_al_errors() (declared in openal.h, defined here) is deleted
entirely along with every call site -- there is no OpenAL error state
left to dump. The slot-polling thread and mutex/condvar machinery are
unrelated to OpenAL/SDL2_sound and are untouched; AudioPlayer/
SDLDecoder/OpenAlSource keep working exactly as their own stubs define.

Verified standalone: openalsource.cpp.obj and audio_core.cpp.obj both
compile clean, zero errors (audio_core.cpp.obj has one pre-existing,
unrelated warning -- audio_core_entry() declared static but never
defined, because AGS_DISABLE_THREADS is unconditionally set for DOS by
patch 0001 and compiles out that function's only definition; not
introduced by this patch, not touched). Also re-verified
audioplayer.cpp.obj (consumes OpenAlSource, not touched by this patch)
still compiles clean.

Full make build-ags re-run: the openal.h blocker is fully gone. A new,
previously unreached and previously undocumented error now surfaces --
Engine/media/video/videoplayer.h:171, invalid conversion from int to
SDL_AudioFormat -- masked until now by this file's own openal.h error
(it includes openalsource.h). Not fixed by this patch; a fresh gap,
handled as its own patch (0024) with its own commit and its own
PATCH-SEQUENCE.md row, per this repo's "never silently" convention for
document corrections.
